-- title:
--   Queue and scan deadlines from depth
-- statement:
--   For a board on a positive cycle, assign position $i$ deadline zero if its backward depth is zero, and otherwise $(n-1)(b_i-1)+i$, where $b_i$ is that depth. The queue deadline is the maximum over positions. The scan deadline is $(n-1)$ plus the queue deadline of the board after $n-1$ sweep steps, minus one. All arithmetic here is natural, including truncated subtraction. These quantities specify depth based time budgets without themselves asserting completion by those times.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/DeadlinePrice.lean#L9-L16

